### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.test.tsx`

- **IMPLEMENT**:
  1. Extend the `TerminalView` mock (lines 12-28):
     - Add to its props type: `handleRef?: { current: unknown }`, `ctrlArmed?(): boolean`, `onCtrlUsed?(): void`, `onPrefixData?(d: string): boolean`.
     - When `p.handleRef` is set, assign `p.handleRef.current = { input: (d: string) => inputs.push([p.id, d]), focus() {}, appCursor: () => false };`.
     - Record `if (p.ctrlArmed) ctrlArmeds.set(p.id, p.ctrlArmed);`, `if (p.onCtrlUsed) ctrlUseds.set(p.id, p.onCtrlUsed);` and `if (p.onPrefixData) prefixDatas.set(p.id, p.onPrefixData);`.
     - Declare (at the top of the file, next to `keyFilters`) `const inputs: [string, string][] = []`, `const ctrlArmeds = new Map<string, () => boolean>()`, `const ctrlUseds = new Map<string, () => void>()` and `const prefixDatas = new Map<string, (d: string) => boolean>()`. Clear all four in `beforeEach` (`inputs.length = 0`).
     - Keep the existing `keyFilters`, buttons, `taps` and `data-echo` behaviour.
  2. If `stubCoarse` doesn't exist yet, add it: `vi.stubGlobal("matchMedia", vi.fn((q: string) => ({ matches: on && q === COARSE, media: q, addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {} })))`.
  3. New `describe("extra keys")` tests. Focus a terminal with `act(() => (screen.getByText("sim-exit-t2") as HTMLButtonElement).focus())`. That button sits inside `.tp-body`; real `focus()` fires `focusin`. Don't click it, because clicking simulates an exit.
     - "with a coarse pointer and a focused terminal the row shows and sends keys": `stubCoarse(true); serve(); mount(); fireEvent.click(await screen.findByTestId("terminal-item-t2"));`. Then:
       - before focus there is no `extra-keys`;
       - after the focus `screen.getByTestId("extra-keys")` exists, and the page `page-terminals` className contains `xk`;
       - `fireEvent.click(screen.getByTestId("xk-esc"))` makes `inputs` contain `["t2", "\x1b"]`, and `xk-up` gives `["t2", "\x1b[A"]`.
     - "xk-prefix arms the prefix": after the setup above, `fireEvent.click(screen.getByTestId("xk-prefix"))`. Then `screen.getByTestId("prefix-hint")` exists and `keyFilters.get("t2")!(new KeyboardEvent("keydown", { key: "n" }))` is `false`, as in the prefix test at lines 300-312. Then `let swallowed = false; act(() => { swallowed = prefixDatas.get("t2")!("n"); });` and `swallowed` is true, and `await screen.findByRole("dialog", { name: "New terminal" })` opens.
     - "sticky Ctrl turns on with xk-ctrl and clears after one use or a pane change":
       - with the setup above, click `xk-ctrl`. It has `aria-pressed="true"` and `ctrlArmeds.get("t2")!()` is `true`;
       - `act(() => ctrlUseds.get("t2")!())` (what TerminalView calls after applying Ctrl). Then `xk-ctrl` has `aria-pressed="false"` and `ctrlArmeds.get("t2")!()` is `false`;
       - click `xk-ctrl` again (pressed), then `fireEvent.click(screen.getByTestId("layout-2"))` and `fireEvent.mouseDown(screen.getByTestId("pane-2"))`. The focused pane changes, and `xk-ctrl` has `aria-pressed="false"`. DOM focus is still in pane 1's button, so the row stays.
     - "no extra keys with a fine pointer": `stubCoarse(false)`, the same open and focus. Then `screen.queryByTestId("extra-keys")` is `null`.
     - "the row hides when focus leaves the terminals": with `stubCoarse(true)`, focus the terminal as above, then `act(() => (screen.getByTestId("new-terminal") as HTMLButtonElement).focus())`. That is the sidebar's Plain terminal button, outside `.terms-grid`. Then `screen.queryByTestId("extra-keys")` is `null`.
- **GOTCHA**:
  - `fireEvent.focus` does not trigger React's `onFocus` (React listens to `focusin`). Use real `.focus()` inside `act`, or `fireEvent.focusIn`.
  - The stub must match only `COARSE`, so `NARROW` stays false and the wide layout stays.
